    "knowledge_point": "Computing Components of the Real and Imaginary Parts of a Complex Matrix",
    "problem": "If $\\,\\text{Re}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,\\text{Im}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}e & f \\\\ g & h\\end{aligned}]\\,$ are the real and imaginary parts of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-3\\text{i} & 5\\text{i} \\\\ -4 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\,$ then what is the value of $ah-cf?$",
    "worked_solution": "For the given matrix $A,$ we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-3\\text{i} & 5\\text{i} \\\\ -4 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0-3\\text{i} & 0+5\\text{i} \\\\ -4+0\\text{i} & 5+0\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(A)}+\\text{i}{{[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(A)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $a=0,c=-4,f=5$ and $h=0.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nah-cf=0\\cdot 0-(-4)\\cdot 5=20.\n$$",
